<%= generated_header("Postfix virtual_mailbox_domains — the domains this server is the FINAL DESTINATION for.") -%>
#
# A domain listed here is a domain Postfix will NOT do an MX lookup for. If the
# recipient is not in vmailbox, the mail is rejected — it is never relayed on.
# So a domain belongs here only if its MX record actually points at this server.
#
# Plesk listed all six of its domains here while three of them (djtim.eu,
# rijschool-mos.nl, mos-safeguards.com) have MX elsewhere, which is why this
# server currently bounces its own mail to those domains.
#
# The value column is ignored by Postfix — only the presence of the key matters
# — but it is written as "<domain>/" because that is byte-for-byte the shape the
# running Postfix already accepts.
<% domain_rows.each do |row| -%>
<%= row[:name] %>	<%= row[:name] %>/
<% end -%>
<% if domain_rows.empty? -%>
# (no domain accepts local delivery)
<% end -%>
